        "content": "<p>alexcrichton opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/14845\">issue #14845</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This input:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"wasm\"><pre><span></span><code>(module\n  (type $s (struct (field i32)))\n  (func (export \"main\") (param $n i32) (result anyref)\n    (loop $l\n      (drop (struct.new $s (i32.const 0x30)))\n      (br_if $l (local.tee $n (i32.sub (local.get $n) (i32.const 1)))))\n    (ref.null any)))\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>fails with:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"cp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cargo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">D</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">guest</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">debug</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"n\">invoke</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">main</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">../</span><span class=\"n\">wasmtime</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">vuln</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">triage</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">bug</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">triage</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"mi\">0163</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">gc</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">guest</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">debug</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">cold</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">libcall</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">wrong</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">stack</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">shape</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10000</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Finished</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">`</span><span class=\"n\">dev</span><span class=\"err\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">profile</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">unoptimized</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">debuginfo</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">target</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">0.10</span><span class=\"n\">s</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"n\">Running</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">`</span><span class=\"n\">target</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">debug</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">wasmtime</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">D</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">guest</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">debug</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"n\">invoke</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">main</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">../</span><span class=\"n\">wasmtime</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">vuln</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">triage</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">bug</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">triage</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"mi\">0163</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">gc</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">guest</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">debug</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">cold</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">libcall</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">wrong</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">stack</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">shape</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10000</span><span class=\"err\">`</span>\n<span class=\"n\">warning</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">`</span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"n\">invoke</span><span class=\"err\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">function</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">that</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">takes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arguments</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">experimental</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">and</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">may</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">break</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">future</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">thread</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">'</span><span class=\"na\">main</span><span class=\"o\">'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">408509</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">panicked</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">crates</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">wasmtime</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">src</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">runtime</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">vm</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">gc</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">enabled</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">copying</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">rs</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">1044</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">13</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"nc\">assertion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">failed</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">self</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">heap</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">is_in_idle_space</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">old_index</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">note</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">run</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">`</span><span class=\"n\">RUST_BACKTRACE</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"err\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">environment</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">display</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">backtrace</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>An LLM summary, if helpful, is:</p>\n<p>&lt;details&gt;</p>\n<p>With <code>Config::guest_debug(true)</code> and the copying collector, a GC that<br>\nhappens inside a libcall (for example the <code>gc_alloc_raw</code> slow path of<br>\n<code>struct.new</code>) traces the frame's debug state slot using the stack shape of<br>\nsome <em>earlier</em> program point. That can make the collector treat a live<br>\nnon-reference operand, such as an <code>i32</code>, as a GC root.</p>\n<h3>Reproduction</h3>\n<p><code>gc-libcall.wat</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"WebAssembly\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">module</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">type</span> <span class=\"nv\">$s</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">struct</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">field</span> <span class=\"kt\">i32</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">func</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">export</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"main\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">param</span> <span class=\"nv\">$n</span> <span class=\"kt\">i32</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">result</span> <span class=\"err\">anyref</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">loop</span> <span class=\"nv\">$l</span>\n      <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">drop</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">struct.new</span> <span class=\"nv\">$s</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">i32.const</span> <span class=\"mf\">0x30)</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n      <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">br_if</span> <span class=\"nv\">$l</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">local.tee</span> <span class=\"nv\">$n</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">i32.sub</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">local.get</span> <span class=\"nv\">$n</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">i32.const</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">)))))</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">ref.null</span> <span class=\"err\">any</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>With a debug build of the CLI at bytecodealliance/wasmtime@68b32edee9 (GC,<br>\nfunction references and the copying collector are all on by default):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"cp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wasmtime</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">D</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">guest</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">debug</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"n\">invoke</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">main</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">gc</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">libcall</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10000</span>\n<span class=\"n\">thread</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">'</span><span class=\"na\">main</span><span class=\"o\">'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">panicked</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">crates</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">wasmtime</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">src</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">runtime</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">vm</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">gc</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">enabled</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">copying</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">rs</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">1044</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">13</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"nc\">assertion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">failed</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">self</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">heap</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">is_in_idle_space</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">old_index</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"cp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wasmtime</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"n\">invoke</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">main</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">gc</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">libcall</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10000</span>\n<span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">null</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">anyref</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The argument must be large enough for an allocation to trigger a GC: here<br>\n2045 iterations still pass and 2046 panic.</p>\n<p>The value that ends up treated as a root is the guest's <code>i32</code> operand, so<br>\nother constants fail differently. With <code>0x100</code>, the 49.0.3 release CLI<br>\naborts with a panic at <code>crates/environ/src/gc.rs:523:32</code>. A release build of<br>\n<code>main</code> showed no visible effect for <code>0x30</code>, <code>0x100</code> or <code>0x7fffffff</code>. But it<br>\nstill reads a guest-chosen value as a GC reference, so wrong results are<br>\npossible.</p>\n<h3>Cause</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>When guest debugging is on, the frame table records a program point (a<br>\n  PC plus the state slot's stack shape) only for instructions with debug<br>\n  tags. Today those are Wasm-level calls (<code>attach_tags</code>,<br>\n<code>crates/cranelift/src/func_environ.rs:2639</code>), the per-operator<br>\n  breakpoint (<code>before_translate_operator</code>, <code>func_environ.rs:5324</code>) and the<br>\n  trap <code>raise</code> libcall (<code>crates/cranelift/src/trap.rs</code>). All other libcalls<br>\n  are emitted without tags. That includes <code>gc_alloc_raw</code><br>\n  (<code>emit_gc_raw_alloc</code>, <code>crates/cranelift/src/func_environ/gc.rs:238</code>),<br>\n  which is in a cold block after the function body.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>During a GC, <code>trace_wasm_stack_frame</code><br>\n  (<code>crates/wasmtime/src/runtime/store/gc.rs:760</code>) calls <code>gc_refs_in_frame</code><br>\n  (<code>crates/wasmtime/src/runtime/debug.rs:839</code>). That looks up the return<br>\n  address with <code>FrameTable::find_program_point(pc, FrameInstPos::Post)</code><br>\n  (<code>crates/environ/src/frame_table.rs:192</code>).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>An untagged libcall's return address has no entry, so the binary search<br>\n  falls back to the nearest preceding program point (<code>Err(idx) if idx &gt; 0\n  =&gt; idx - 1</code>, <code>frame_table.rs:203</code>). Since the libcall is in the same<br>\n  function, the function-start check doesn't reject that point.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>In the reproducer, that point is the function's final <code>end</code>, whose stack<br>\n  shape is <code>[anyref]</code>. But the slot's stack entry 0 holds the <code>i32</code> operand<br>\n  of <code>struct.new</code>, which was flushed there before the operator's breakpoint.<br>\n  The copying collector then tries to forward it.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The normal stack maps aren't affected; this is only about the debug state<br>\nslot. Any libcall that can GC has the same problem, not just <code>gc_alloc_raw</code>:<br>\nfor example other allocation paths, explicit collections, table or array<br>\ngrowth, and epoch or fuel yields that run host code.</p>\n<h3>Possible fix</h3>\n<p>One option is to tag every call that doesn't already have tags with the<br>\ntags of the breakpoint of the operator it was emitted for. The state slot's<br>\noperand stack is only flushed between operators (<code>update_state_slot_stack</code>,<br>\n<code>func_environ.rs:1358</code>, called from <code>after_translate_operator</code>). So for<br>\nthe whole of an operator's translation, the slot has the shape recorded at<br>\nthat operator's breakpoint. For example:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">// In `before_translate_operator`, after setting the breakpoint's tags:</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">breakpoints</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">insert</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">builder</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">srcloc</span><span class=\"p\">(),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">// At the end of the function (e.g. from `finish_debug_metadata`), for each</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">// `call`, `call_indirect`, `try_call` or `try_call_indirect` without tags:</span>\n<span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">Some</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">bp</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">breakpoints</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"n\">func</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">srcloc</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"p\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">func</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">debug_tags</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">clone_tags</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"n\">bp</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>With that, the reproducer passes. <code>tests/all</code> and <code>tests/disas</code> also pass;<br>\n<code>tests/disas/debug-exceptions.wat</code> only gains <code>debug frame state</code> lines on<br>\nlibcalls.</p>\n<p>Making <code>find_program_point(.., Post)</code> require an exact match, so the<br>\nframe contributes no debug roots, isn't enough with a moving collector. The<br>\nstate slot's references wouldn't be updated, and the debugger would later<br>\nread stale values.</p>\n<p>Open question: calls emitted before the first operator (the function-entry<br>\nstack-limit check and fuel/epoch setup) have no breakpoint to copy tags<br>\nfrom, and would stay untagged. If one of them can GC while the state slot<br>\nholds reference-typed parameters, it needs its own program point. I haven't<br>\nchecked this.</p>\n<p>&lt;/details&gt;<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 633112878,
